oq-2 evidence: whole-module gremlins dry-run attempt, and the baseline
per-package coverage-gathering timings this spike's oq-2 table draws its
"bounded by baseline timing" figures from.

Command (scratch worktree, detached at e963f4d0):
  $ gremlins unleash --dry-run --diff b810c302 --output /tmp/gremlins-dryrun-diff.json .
  exit=1
  wall clock: 807.00s user, 973.65s system, 292% cpu, 10:09.06 total

This run was an attempt to scope gremlins to the touched-files diff over
the WHOLE module in one invocation (path "."), superseded in this spike's
own methodology by the per-touched-package approach oq-2's README section
describes (this single invocation's coverage-gathering phase runs every
package's own test suite once, exactly like `go test -cover ./...`, and
that is expensive/fragile at whole-module scope — see below). Kept as
evidence anyway because its output is the source of every "baseline pass"
timing this spike quotes for the six packages it could not mutation-test
directly this session, and because its failure is itself a real, useful
finding.

Reduction: gremlins' own progress output uses carriage returns, not
newlines, between spinner frames; the raw capture (244 lines after
normalizing \r to \n) is almost entirely that spinner noise. Kept below:
every one of Go's own `ok`/`FAIL` per-package result lines (102 total —
every package `go test`'s own coverage pass touched before the run gave
up), verbatim and in original order; both failures' own diagnostic
output; and the final fatal line. Nothing else was removed (there was
nothing else — the spinner frames carry no information `wc -l` or `grep`
can distinguish from each other).

