Both failures are pre-existing in this wave-1 branch's own tree at
e963f4d0, discovered as a side effect of attempting a whole-module
`--diff` scope, not introduced by this spike and not touched by it.
align's is a load-sensitivity gap in the product's own test suite (a
hardcoded 1s subprocess deadline), independently interesting to the
process-hardening effort but out of this spike's scope to fix. sealedexec's
"stale witness source cmd/verdi/context.go" / "...internal/policyconflict/
service.go" is consistent with the wave-1 diff itself having edited both
files (they are on this diff's own touched-file list) without regenerating
a witness fixture that tracks their content — also out of scope to fix
here, but worth the implementing feature's attention if it inherits this
branch.
